      "side": 1,
      "message": "Sorry I should have been more clear: it is now API approval policy to only make @SystemApi the APIs that are in any way sensitive, and should be behind a system permission. Correct, you will find existing @SystemApi that are not guarded, but those are older, and all Android R @SystemApi are guarded.\nIF this doesn\u0027t apply, then the API is candidate for entering the SDK and be made public. The thing I don\u0027t understand here is that typically MediaPlayer users do not manage the buffering, it is handled internally by MediaPlayer. So what is the use case here? Who would be using this API and for what purpose?",
